details:
(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of migrant workforce employed in Kerala;
(b) the details of Central schemes implemented for their social security, health insurance and welfare;
(c) the number of migrant workers registered on e-Shram portal in the State; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure access to social security benefits, safe working conditions and portability of welfare schemes?

(a) the details of skill development programmes implemented by Government during the last five years, scheme-wise;
(b) the number of candidates trained, certified and placed in employment under these programmes, year-wise and State-wise, including Kerala;
(c) whether Government has conducted any assessment of the long-term employment outcomes and retention rates of candidates placed through these programmes;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the measures taken to improve job creation, industry linkages and placement opportunities under skill development initiatives?

(a) the number of Pradhan Mantri Bhartiya Janaushadhi Kendras functioning in the country and in Kerala, district-wise;
(b) the details of medicines supplied and the savings accrued to consumers during the last five years;
(c) whether any proposals for opening new Kendras in underserved areas of Kerala are under consideration; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure uninterrupted availability and quality of medicines at Janaushadhi Kendras?

(a) whether Government has assessed the availability and timely supply of subsidised fertilizers, including urea, DAP, NPK and other major ones to farmers during the current agricultural season;
(b) if so, the details thereof including State-wise requirement, allocation and supply of fertilizers during the current season with special reference to Kerala;
(c) whether any shortages or delays in fertilizer supply have been reported during the last two years and the reasons therefor; and
(d) the measures taken to ensure adequate availability of fertilizers at affordable and notified prices and prevent black marketing and diversion?

(a) whether NITI Aayog has conducted any assessment of regional disparities in economic growth, infrastructure and human development across States during the last five years;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the State of Kerala's position on key development indicators;
(c) whether Government proposes any targeted strategy or special assistance to address inter-State development disparities; and
(d) the details of projects or initiatives recommended by NITI Aayog for Kerala during the last five years and their implementation status?

(a) whether Government has fixed the Minimum Support Price (MSP) for paddy for the current Kharif and Rabi marketing seasons, if so, the details thereof, including the MSP announced during the last five years;
(b) whether Government has assessed that the prevailing MSP is adequate to meet the cost of cultivation and provide remunerative returns to paddy farmers, particularly in Kerala, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the details of Central funds released and utilised during the last five years for the procurement of paddy and for schemes supporting paddy cultivation in Kerala, scheme-wise, year-wise?

(a) the State/UT-wise unemployment rate among educated persons, including graduates and above, during each of the last five years, as per the latest available official data;
(b) the number of educated unemployed persons registered with employment exchanges and other Government employment portals during the said period, State/UT-wise;
(c) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the factors contributing to educated unemployment in the country and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken by Government to enhance employment opportunities, improve employability and reduce educated unemployment, particularly among youth and women?

(a) the total expenditure incurred by Union Government on higher education during each of the last five years, year-wise;
(b) State-wise/UT-wise details of Central funds allocated and released for higher education during the said period, indicating the major schemes under which such assistance was provided;
(c) whether there has been any change in the pattern or quantum of Central funding for higher education during the last five years, if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; and
(d) the measures taken by Government to ensure equitable and adequate funding for higher education institutions across all States and Union Territories?

(a) State-wise/UT-wise number of Government colleges, including Government degree colleges, presently functioning in the country;
(b) the number of Government colleges established and the number closed, merged or discontinued during each of the last five years, State-wise/UT-wise, along with the reasons therefor;
(c) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the impact of such closures or mergers on students' access to higher education, particularly in rural, tribal and underserved areas, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken by Government to strengthen Government colleges and improve equitable access to affordable higher education across the country?

(a) whether Government has assessed the average waiting time for diagnosis and treatment of cancer patients in Government hospitals across the country;
(b) the State/UT-wise number of Regional Cancer Centres and Government cancer treatment facilities;
(c) whether there is a shortage of oncologists, radiotherapy equipment and chemotherapy facilities, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to strengthen affordable and timely cancer care, particularly in rural and underserved areas?

(a) whether Government has taken steps to modernise the national statistical system for improving the quality, coverage and timeliness of official statistics;
(b) details of major national surveys and statistical reports due for release during the last three years, indicating their scheduled and actual dates of publication;
(c) whether any surveys or reports have been delayed, if so, the reasons thereof;
(d) initiatives taken to strengthen digital data collection, data quality assurance and coordination with States/UTs; and
(e) measures taken to enhance public access, transparency and reliability of official statistics?

(a) whether NITI Aayog has prepared any long-term national development strategy or roadmap for achieving the goals of Viksit Bharat @2047;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the major sector-wise targets and milestones;
(c) whether State Governments have been consulted in the preparation and implementation of the roadmap, if so, the details thereof;
(d) the mechanism evolved for monitoring progress and evaluating outcomes; and
(e) the measures taken to ensure balanced regional development and reduce inter-State disparities under the roadmap?

(a) the State/UT-wise details of funds allocated, sanctioned, released and utilised under the Viksit Bharat – Guarantee for Rozgar and Ajeevika Mission (Gramin) (VB-G RAM G) Scheme during the current financial year and each of the last three financial years;
(b) the details of pending Central releases, if any, along with the reasons therefor;
(c) whether any State/UT has reported delays in the release of funds affecting wage payments and implementation of the Scheme, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to ensure the timely release of funds and effective implementation of the VB-G RAM G Scheme across the country?

(a) the minimum wages notified for various categories of workers, including unskilled, semi-skilled, skilled and highly skilled workers, as on date, State/UT-wise;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any review of adequacy of the existing minimum wages, in view of inflation and the rising cost of living and if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government proposes to revise or increase the minimum wages, including through the implementation of floor wages under the Code on Wages, 2019 and if so, the details and likely timeline thereof; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure compliance with minimum wage provisions across the country?

(a) the number of Central Government pensioners residing in the State of Kerala;
(b) the number of grievances received from the State through the Centralized Public Grievance Redress and Monitoring System during the last five years and the percentage of grievances disposed of within the prescribed timeline;
(c) whether Government has received complaints on delays in pension revision, family pension disbursement or digital life certificate processing in the State;
(d) the steps taken to streamline pension disbursement and grievance redressal mechanisms for pensioners there; and
(e) the details of proposals to establish pension facilitation centres in the States with a high concentration of pensioners?

(a) the number of employees laid off by Information Technology (IT) companies during each of the last three years, company-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) whether Government has assessed the reasons for increase in layoffs in IT sector and if so, the details thereof;
(c) the measures taken by Government to protect the interests of affected employees, including support for re-skilling and re-employment; and
(d) whether Government proposes any policy or regulatory measures to prevent arbitrary layoffs and promote employment stability in the IT sector and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the socio-economic conditions and livelihood challenges faced by traditional fishermen in Kerala during the last five years, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the details of financial assistance, livelihood support and welfare benefits provided to fishermen in Kerala under various Central Government schemes during the period;
(c) whether Government has taken note of the increasing operational costs, declining fish catch and the impact of climate change on the income of fishermen in the State; and
(d) the measures taken by Government to improve the income, social security and livelihood opportunities of fishermen in Kerala?

(a) the total amount of Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) funds spent in the State of Kerala during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) Kerala’s rank among States in terms of CSR expenditure during the said period;
(c) the details of CSR spending in Kerala, including health, education, disaster relief, environmental sustainability and livelihood development, sector-wise;
(d) whether Government has assessed equitable distribution of CSR funds across districts in Kerala, including tribal and coastal regions; and
(e) whether any mechanism exists to encourage companies operating in Kerala to undertake CSR projects within the State?

(a) the total number of houses sanctioned, completed and occupied under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban) during each of the last three years, State/UT-wise;
(b) the total funds allocated, released and utilised under the scheme during the said period, State/UT-wise;
(c) the number of beneficiaries belonging to Scheduled Castes, Scheduled Tribes, Other Backward Classes, minorities and women under the scheme;
(d) whether Government has identified delays in the completion of sanctioned houses, if so, the reasons therefor and the corrective measures taken; and
(e) the targets fixed for the construction of houses under the scheme during the next three years, State/UT-wise?

(a) the peak electricity demand and peak demand met in the country during each of the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the present installed power generation capacity, source-wise, including thermal, hydro, nuclear and renewable energy;
(c) whether Government has assessed the country's power generation requirements over the next ten years in view of increasing industrialisation, urbanisation and electrification, if so, the details thereof;
(d) the measures taken to strengthen transmission infrastructure and prevent power shortages during periods of peak demand; and
(e) the steps taken by Government to ensure an affordable, reliable and sustainable electricity supply across the country?

(a) initiatives undertaken by Government to promote the use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in agriculture and farmers' welfare;
(b) details of AI-based projects implemented during the last five years, indicating their objectives, areas of application and States/UTs covered;
(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of AI-based technologies on crop productivity, precision farming, pest and disease management, weather forecasting and farmers' income, if so, the details thereof;
(d) funds allocated and utilised for AI-based agricultural initiatives during the last five years; and
(e) measures taken to enhance farmers' access to AI-enabled technologies, digital advisory services and capacity-building programmes, particularly for small and marginal farmers?

(a) the amount allocated, released and utilised under the Indian Community Welfare Fund (ICWF) during each of the last five years, country-wise;
(b) the number of Indian nationals who received assistance from the fund during the said period; 
(c) the criteria and procedure for extending assistance under the fund;
(d) whether Government has undertaken any review of the functioning and adequacy of the fund in meeting the welfare needs of Indian nationals abroad and if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the measures taken to strengthen the fund and improve awareness, accessibility and timely delivery of assistance to Indians in distress overseas?

(a) the State-wise/UT-wise Infant Mortality Rate (IMR), Under-Five Mortality Rate (U5MR) and Neonatal Mortality Rate (NMR) in the country, as per the latest available data;
(b) the trends in these indicators during each of the last three years, State-wise/UT-wise;
(c) the States/UTs with mortality rates higher than the national average and the reasons identified for it;
(d) the details of Central assistance provided to States/UTs for reducing child mortality during the last three years, State-wise/UT-wise; and
(e) the measures taken by Government to achieve the Sustainable Development Goals relating to child survival and reduce regional disparities in child mortality?

(a) the details of all major ports in the country, indicating their ownership, management structure and operating model;
(b) whether any major ports or port terminals have been leased, privatised or developed under the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) model during the last ten years; if so, the details thereof;
(c) the revenue earned by Government from such ports during the last five years, port-wise;
(d) the measures taken by Government to ensure transparency, competition and public interest in the management of major ports; and
(e) whether Government proposes any changes in ownership or management structure of major ports, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of the ownership, concession and operational model of the Vizhinjam International Deepwater Multipurpose Seaport, including the respective roles and responsibilities of the Central Government, Government of Kerala and the private concessionaire;
(b) the period of concession agreement, the revenue-sharing mechanism and the obligations of each stakeholder under the agreement;
(c) the total investment made by the Central Government, Government of Kerala and the private concessionaire;
(d) the projected cargo handling capacity, expected revenue and employment generation from the port; and 
(e) the measures taken by Government to ensure transparency, regulatory oversight and protection of public interest in the operation of the port?

(a) the retail price of a 14.2 kg domestic LPG cylinder during each of the last five years, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) the details of subsidies provided on domestic LPG cylinders during the said period, year-wise;
(c) the factors responsible for the increase or decrease in LPG prices from time to time; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to make domestic cooking gas affordable for economically weaker and middle-income households?

(a) the population of minority communities in Kerala and their percentage in the State's population, as per the latest available data;
(b) number of beneficiaries from Kerala under various minority scholarship schemes during the last five years, scheme-wise;
(c) whether any such schemes have been reduced, discontinued or restructured, if so, the details thereof;
(d) funds allocated and released to Kerala for the Ministry's schemes during the last five years; and
(e) steps taken to ensure timely scholarship disbursal and skill development support for minority youth in the State?

(a) whether Government recognizes Theyyam of North Kerala as an important form of India’s intangible cultural heritage;
(b) whether any proposal has been submitted to include Theyyam in UNESCO’s Representative List of Intangible Cultural Heritage and if so, the status thereof;
(c) the details of financial assistance provided to Theyyam artists, troupes and cultural institutions in North Kerala during the last five years, year-wise;
(d) whether Government proposes to establish a dedicated cultural centre, museum or research institute for documentation and preservation of Theyyam traditions; and
(e) the steps taken to provide welfare support, insurance and pension benefits to traditional Theyyam performers?

(a) whether the objectives envisaged under the Indo–US Nuclear Agreement of 2008 have been achieved;
(b) the details of civil nuclear cooperation agreements signed with other countries following the Nuclear Suppliers Group (NSG) waiver granted to India;
(c) the extent to which the agreements have contributed to enhancement of India’s nuclear power generation capacity;
(d) whether any foreign nuclear reactors have been commissioned or are under construction in India, pursuant to such agreements;
(e) whether any constraints, including issues relating to nuclear liability, have affected the implementation of such agreements; and
(f) the overall strategic and economic impact of such agreements on India’s global standing?

(a) the total number of road accidents and fatalities reported on National Highways in Kerala during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the number of accident-prone “black spots” identified on National Highways in the State and the details of corrective measures taken;
(c) whether the ongoing widening and development works on National Highways, including NH-66, have led to increased accident risks and traffic disruptions;
(d) the funds allocated and released for road safety measures on National Highways in Kerala during the last five years; and
(e) the steps taken to enhance highway safety through improved signage, service roads, pedestrian crossings and emergency response systems?

(a) Kerala’s ranking in major national development indices, including the Sustainable Development Goals (SDG) Index and Multidimensional Poverty Index, during the last three years;
(b) whether any district in the State of Kerala have been identified under the Aspirational Districts Programme and the progress achieved therein;
(c) details of policy support and technical assistance provided by NITI Aayog to the State during the last three years;
(d) whether the Government of Kerala has sought special consideration in view of its ageing population and climate vulnerability; and
(e) steps taken to ensure balanced regional development within the State, particularly in Northern districts?

(a) the total value of textile and handloom exports from Kannur and Kasaragod districts of Kerala during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the major export destinations for textile products from these districts;
(c) whether Government has provided assistance under schemes such as the National Handloom Development Programme, Production Linked Incentive (PLI) Scheme or any export promotion schemes to textile units in Kannur and Kasaragod;
(d) the details of textile clusters or export parks functioning in the said districts and the support extended thereto; and
(e) the steps taken by Government to enhance global competitiveness of handloom and home textile products from north Kerala?

(a) whether Government has set up any Free Animal Health Camps for farmers, herdsman and shepherd, stockman etc, in the last three years;
(b) if so, details of these camps, State-wise, along with the dates and number and type of animals enrolled;
(c) if not, reasons therefor; and
(d) details of diseases identified, treatment, medicine, vaccines and tests provided to the animals?
BPN

(a) whether Government has ensured adequate supply of fertilizers to the State of Kerala particularly during peak agricultural seasons of the last five years;
(b) the quantity of urea, DAP, and other major fertilizers allocated and supplied to Kerala during the said period, year-wise;
(c) the present operational status and production capacity of Fertilisers and Chemicals Travancore Limited (FACT), Kochi;
(d) whether Government proposes any modernisation or expansion plan for FACT to enhance domestic fertilizer production; and
(e) the steps taken to prevent shortage and price fluctuation of fertilizers affecting farmers in Kerala?

(a) whether the Centre of Excellence established at Indian Institute of Technology, Delhi has achieved its intended goals in areas related to AYUSH research, innovation and integrative health solutions;
(b) if so, the details of aims, goals and vision of the Union Government, the key milestones achieved till date and the measurable outcomes;
(c) whether Government is collaborating with national and international institutions to assess the sector-specific needs of AyurTech; and
(d) if so, the details thereof of the collaboration pursued post 2023?
bs

(a) the number of central sector infrastructure projects that have reported cost overruns and time delays as of the quarter ending December, 2025;
(b) whether Government has updated the Sustainable Development Goals (SDG) National Indicator Framework for 2026; and
(c) the latest Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS) data on urban unemployment for the January, 2026 quarter compared to the same quarter in 2025?

(a) the total power allocation from Central Generating Stations to the State of Kerala during the last five years, year-wise details;
(b) whether the Central Government has received any request from the State for additional power allocation and the status thereof;
(c) details of central assistance provided to the State for strengthening transmission infrastructure and grid modernization during the last five years;
(d) status of renewable energy projects, including solar and wind projects, supported by the Central Government in the State; and
(e) whether Government proposes any special measures for States like Kerala which are highly dependent on hydropower and vulnerable to monsoon variations?
bs

(a) the details of railway infrastructure projects currently under implementation in north Kerala, including line doubling, electrification, station redevelopment and new line proposals;
(b) the status of track doubling and capacity enhancement works in the Shoranur–Mangaluru corridor;
(c) whether Government has assessed the increasing passenger and freight congestion in north Kerala, if so, the details thereof;
(d) the funds allocated and expended for railway infrastructure development in north Kerala during the last five years, year-wise; and
(e) whether Government proposes to sanction any new projects or accelerate pending works to improve rail connectivity and reduce travel time in the region?
bs

(a) the total value of exports from Kerala during the last five years, sector-wise, including marine products, spices, coir, rubber and IT services;
(b) Kerala’s rank among States in terms of merchandise and services exports during the said period;
(c) the details of industrial corridors, export parks or Special Economic Zones (SEZs) approved or operational in Kerala;
(d) whether Government proposes to leverage the operationalisation of Vizhinjam International Seaport to boost export-oriented industries in Kerala, if so, the steps taken in this regard; and
(e) the assistance provided to MSMEs in Kerala under Central schemes to enhance export competitiveness?

(a) whether Government has assessed the impact of climate change in Kerala, particularly with regard to recurring floods, landslides, coastal erosion and sea-level rise;
(b) the details of climate vulnerability assessments conducted there during the last five years;
(c) the details of funds allocated and released to the State under the National Adaptation Fund for Climate Change (NAFCC), State Action Plan on Climate Change (SAPCC) and other climate-related schemes during those years, year-wise; and
(d) whether the State has sought additional financial assistance in view of its high climate vulnerability and if so, the status thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken note that Kerala has one of the highest proportions of elderly population in the country;
(b) the details of schemes implemented by the Ministry for welfare of senior citizens in Kerala during the last five years;
(c) the funds allocated and released to Kerala under schemes such as the integrated programme for senior citizens during the said period;
(d) whether any proposal has been received for establishing additional old age homes, geriatric care centres or day-care centres in Kerala, status thereof; and
(e) whether Government propose any special policy intervention for States with rapidly ageing populations such as Kerala?

(a) whether Government has any proposal to direct the State Governments to assess and fix a minimum number of beneficiaries to be linked with each Fair Price Shop (FPS) to ensure its economic viability;
(b) whether Government is aware that in several States, new Fair Price Shop licences are being issued without assessing the viability of the existing shops;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) whether Government proposes to issue guidelines to States to conduct a viability assessment of existing Fair Price Shops before granting licences for new shops?

(a) the details of the price of petrol and diesel during the last three years State-wise;
(b) whether Government is aware of the inter-State variation in the price of petrol and diesel across the country;
(c) whether Government is aware of the negative impact of this inter-State variation on commerce and industry in each State; and
(d) if so, whether Government has any plan to bring petroleum products under GST?

(a) whether Government has conducted any study to assess the impact of Artificial Intelligence (AI) on the sustainability of Indian industries;
(b) if so, the positive and negative impact of AI application on the future of Indian industries;
(c) whether Government has initiated any remedial measures to reduce the negative impact of AI in indigenous industries; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?
P

(a) the list of farmers who committed suicide due to debt trap and crop loss, State-wise;
(b) whether there is any methodology to understand the issue of farmers' suicide in the country;
(c) whether Government has set up any commission to understand and prevent the suicide of farmers in the country; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons thereof?

(a) the number of unorganised workers in the country;
(b) the number of unorganised workers protected under social security schemes;
(c) the reasons for huge number of non-protected workers in the unorganised sector; and
(d) whether the Ministry has any plan to initiative any specific programme to provide social security for all the workers in unorganised sector?
bs

(a) whether any pension scheme is currently existing for the construction workers, home-based workers, traders and other unorganised workers;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) if not, whether Government has any plan to implement pension schemes for those workers;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of policies issued under the Pravasi Bharatiya Bima Yojana, as on January 31, 2026;
(b) the State-wise details of emigrant workers who are currently covered under the Yojana, as on January 31, 2026; and
(c) the State-wise details of claims settled under the Yojana, as on January 31, 2026?

(a) the list of Ayush companies that have been identified for selling adulterated Ayurvedic drugs in the country since 2023, State-wise;
(b) the details of the actions taken against the Ayush companies that are identified for selling adulterated Ayurvedic drugs in the country since 2023;
(c) whether Government has adopted any monitoring mechanism to prevent the practice of selling adulterated Ayurvedic drugs; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the contribution of the healthcare sector in our GDP in the last financial year;
(b) the trends in contribution of the healthcare sector in GDP since 2020;
(c) the contribution of private healthcare sector in total GDP and the trends during the period; and
(d) the total number of employees working in both private and public firms operating in the healthcare sector since 2020?

(a) the total number of spinning mills in the country;
(b) the State-wise number of spinning mills that had closed operation since 2020;
(c) the reasons for the closure of spinning mills in the country; and
(d) the initiatives taken by Government to support the spinning mills in the country?

(a) whether Government has a Universal Social Protection plan to provide basic level of social security for all Indian citizens;
(b) if so, the timeline and estimated budget for the initial phase of its implementation; and
(c) the funds allocated for the plan?

(a) whether Government has any scheme or policy to award land rights and ownership titles to Denotified, Nomadic and Semi-Nomadic Tribes (DNTs) who have been occupying the same land for 15-20 years without formal ownership rights;
(b) the number of such landless DNT families identified in the last three years; and
(c) the State-wise progress on issuing land ownership documents to them?

(a) whether the existing coverage of beneficiaries under the National Food Security Act (NFSA) is below the statutory limit of 67 per cent of the population;
(b) the specific steps taken by Government to comply with the mandate of the NFSA and the 2024 directions of the Supreme Court to include more people in the free rations scheme; and
(c) the estimated increase in beneficiary planned for the current financial year?

(a) the number of Primary Health Centres (PHCs) in the private sector or the Public Private Partnership (PPP) model in each State/ UT in the country in the current financial year;
(b) whether Government has made any attempt to evaluate the impact of the privatisation in primary health care; and
(c) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of accidents in coal mines in the country during 2022-25 and the total number of deaths caused by accidents during this period;
(b) the reasons for each accidents and the corrective measures taken after the accidents;
(c) whether the victims were provided compensations, if any; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total number of houses built under the PMAY during the last five years;
(b) the list of the number of houses built under PMAY scheme during the said period,State-wise;
(c) the number of applications pending under the PMAY scheme;
(d) the total amount shared by the Central Government for the construction of houses under the PMAY scheme; and
(e) the total amount spent by each State Government for the scheme?

(a) whether Government aware of the loss of crops due to unexpected climate changes in the country;
(b) if so, the details of the compensation packages extended to farmers for the loss of crops due to unexpected climate change; and
(c) the details of the total funds allotted for climate change induced crop loss in the last three years, State-wise?

(a) the total number of cold storages operational in the country, State-wise along with storage capacity in each State;
(b) whether the existing cold storages are sufficient to meet the demands of the farmers across the country;
(c) if not, the additional capacity required to meet the demands; and
(d) the initiatives taken by Government to increase new cold storages across the country?

(a) whether it is a fact that the Employees Provident Fund Organization (EPFO) is considering enhancement of interest rate for provident fund deposits;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government is planning to make any other change in the EPFO scheme as part of new Labour Code; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has directed all States/UTs to conduct safety audits of school and public facilities buildings used by children in accordance with national safety codes and disaster management guideline;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the details of key parameters likely to be assessed, the standard safety protocols and emergency preparedness measures taken during these audits?

(a) the State-wise list of number of Government and Government-aided schools having digitalised classrooms across the country;
(b) the initiatives taken by Government for digital technology integration in Government schools across the country;
(c) the amount spent for digital technology integration in Government and Government-aided schools across the country for the last five years; and
(d) the State-wise details of the amount disbursed for the last five years for digital technology integration in Government and Government-aided schools?

(a) the list of public and private nursing colleges in the country as of 31st December, 2024, State-wise;
(b) whether Government is planning to set up new nursing colleges in the country;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the rationale behind the selection of States for setting up new nursing colleges?

(a) the list of CGHS centres across the country as of 31st January 2025, State-wise;
(b) whether Government is planning to set up new CGHS centres in Kerala;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of hospitals empanelled under the ECHS in the country State-wise;
(b) whether Government is aware that hospitals under the ECHS are denying essential health care services to ex-servicemen;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether Government has noticed unwillingness of hospitals to remain in the ECHS scheme; and
(e) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor?

(a) the total revenue generated by Indian Railways during 2024-2025;
(b) the revenue generated by Indian Railways from ticket fares during 2024-2025;
(c) whether the Ministry is planning to reinstate the concessions given to senior citizens and women passengers in the coming year;
(d) if so, the tentative date by which the Ministry is planning to reinstate the concessions; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether the current Labour Codes would ensure the social security of unorganised workers in the country;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) whether the Labour Codes include ESIC facilities for unorganized workers; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the State-wise list of manual scavengers in the country as on 31st August 2025;
(b) the State-wise details of the funds allotted for the rehabilitation of manual scavengers in the country as on 31st August, 2025;
(c) the State-wise number of the manual scavengers who received financial support for getting new sources of income; and
(d) the feasibility of the rehabilitation programme for manual scavengers?

(a) the State-wise list of Fair Price Shops in the country as on 30th September 2025;
(b) whether the digitisation of PDS has led to closing down of Fair Price Shops in the country;
(c) whether Government has taken any step to enhance the financial viability of Fair Price Shops in the country; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the PM Internship scheme provides reservation for the SC/ST applicants;
(b) the State-wise list of interns selected from SC/ST communities under the Prime Minister Internship Scheme (PMIS);
